   "source": {
    "label": "Result:Theorem:1",
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "For $T\\geq K^{2.4}$, $\\rho=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\psi=\\frac{T}{K^2}$, the regret $R_T$ for EUCBV satisfies\n\\begin{align*}\n\\E [R_{T}] \\leq &\\sum\\limits_{i\\in \\A :\\Delta_{i} > b}\\bigg\\lbrace \\dfrac{C_0 K^{4}}{T^{\\frac{1}{4}}} + \\bigg(\\Delta_{i}+\\dfrac{320\\sigma_i^2\\log{(\\frac{T\\Delta_{i}^{2}}{K})}}{\\Delta_{i}}\\bigg)\\bigg \\rbrace\\\\ \n  & +\\sum\\limits_{i\\in \\A :0 < \\Delta_{i}\\leq b} \\dfrac{C_2 K^{4}}{T^{\\frac{1}{4}}} + \\max_{i\\in \\A :0 < \\Delta_{i}\\leq b}\\Delta_{i}T.\n\\end{align*}\n\nfor all $b\\geq\\sqrt{\\frac{e}{T}}$ and $C_0, C_2$ are integer constants."
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Regret defined as sum E[z_i(T)] Delta_i, i.e. pseudo-regret. Constants C_0, C_2 unspecified. The proof has questionable steps, but recorded as stated."
  },
